# Violations of tooling/conformance/integrity.ts that are known and owned.
# One per line: project<TAB>rule<TAB>subject<TAB>why. The subject is the
# violation's text, except under cascade-has-root, where it is the blamed
# cause: one entry per unrecorded root, covering every cascade through it;
# and under top-level-cut, where it is what was cut: `the initializer of G`,
# `a statement calling C`, or `module#init`. The cut entries are the ratchet
# toward `nts build` refusing a cut: the day none is left, it can. Under
# location-on-a-token the subject is the diagnostic code: one cause (a
# node's full start used for its token start), so a project names it once.
# Closure numbers and type ids are normalised (ClosureN, <N>, objN). An entry
# that no longer occurs is reported for removal; any violation not listed
# here fails. Entries are in byte order (LC_ALL=C sort), and integrity.ts
# enforces it: insert a new entry where it sorts, never at the end.
examples/a-method-used-as-a-value	unerase-is-built	Generator0	a generator's *declared* class is a shape concrete generator classes are cast to and nothing allocates, which is this tree's convention and predates the erased-call entry: the control emits `(NtsObj_Generator0 *)Rows____pairs(v1)` for the same value. A6 replaced a typed closure return with erase/unerase to the same type, so the cast is one hop further and this rule now asks a question that was always unanswerable. Removed with the generator slot's own work, which is where a declared generator shape gets a descriptor (compiler lane, 2026-09-30)
examples/a-method-used-as-a-value	unerase-is-built	Generator1	a generator's *declared* class is a shape concrete generator classes are cast to and nothing allocates, which is this tree's convention and predates the erased-call entry: the control emits `(NtsObj_Generator0 *)Rows____pairs(v1)` for the same value. A6 replaced a typed closure return with erase/unerase to the same type, so the cast is one hop further and this rule now asks a question that was always unanswerable. Removed with the generator slot's own work, which is where a declared generator shape gets a descriptor (compiler lane, 2026-09-30)
examples/a-private-generator-method-handed-out-as-a-value	unerase-is-built	Generator0	a generator's *declared* class is a shape concrete generator classes are cast to and nothing allocates, which is this tree's convention and predates the erased-call entry: the control emits `(NtsObj_Generator0 *)Rows____pairs(v1)` for the same value. A6 replaced a typed closure return with erase/unerase to the same type, so the cast is one hop further and this rule now asks a question that was always unanswerable. Removed with the generator slot's own work, which is where a declared generator shape gets a descriptor (compiler lane, 2026-09-30)
